<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shivaji of Thanjavur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1855">1855</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> raja of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfoji-ii">Serfoji II</a>, ruling from 1832 to 1855 with the administration already in British hands. When he died in 1855 without a male heir, the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> annexed Thanjavur under the doctrine of lapse. The palace and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saraswati">Saraswati</a> Mahal library remained with the royal family.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shivaji-of-thanjavur.jpg" alt="Shivaji of Thanjavur" width="205" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Royal Ark · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Choladesadhipati_Srimant_Rajasri_Maharaja_Kshatrapati_Sri_Shivaji_Raje_Sahib_Bhonsle_Chhatrapati_Maharaj.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
